.Dd September 25, 2026
.Dt LIBCRYPTODESC 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cryptodesc_mint ,
.Nm cryptodesc_mint_generated ,
.Nm cryptodesc_mint_key ,
.Nm cryptodesc_named_create ,
.Nm cryptodesc_named_lease ,
.Nm cryptodesc_named_rotate ,
.Nm cryptodesc_named_delete ,
.Nm cryptodesc_named_stat ,
.Nm cryptodesc_named_list ,
.Nm cryptodesc_owner_list ,
.Nm cryptodesc_restrict ,
.Nm cryptodesc_revoke ,
.Nm cryptodesc_get_info
.Nd mint and manage kernel crypto session descriptors
.Sh LIBRARY
.Li libcryptodesc
.Pq Fl lcryptodesc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In cryptodesc.h
.Ft int
.Fn cryptodesc_mint "int control_fd" "const struct session2_op *session" "uint32_t rights" "int *descriptor_fd"
.Ft int
.Fn cryptodesc_mint_generated "int control_fd" "const struct session2_op *session" "uint32_t rights" "uint32_t ttl" "int *descriptor_fd"
.Ft int
.Fn cryptodesc_mint_key "int control_fd" "uint32_t type" "uint32_t rights" "uint32_t ttl" "uint8_t public_key[CRYPTODESC_ED25519_PUBLIC_SIZE]" "int *descriptor_fd"
.Ft int
.Fn cryptodesc_named_create "int control_fd" "const char *name" "const char *owner" "const struct session2_op *session" "uint32_t rights" "uint64_t *generation"
.Ft int
.Fn cryptodesc_named_lease "int control_fd" "const char *name" "const char *owner" "uint32_t rights" "uint32_t ttl" "uint64_t *generation" "int *descriptor_fd"
.Ft int
.Fn cryptodesc_named_rotate "int control_fd" "const char *name" "const char *owner" "uint64_t *generation"
.Ft int
.Fn cryptodesc_named_delete "int control_fd" "const char *name" "const char *owner" "uint64_t *generation"
.Ft int
.Fn cryptodesc_named_stat "int control_fd" "const char *name" "const char *owner" "struct cryptodesc_named_stat *stat"
.Ft int
.Fn cryptodesc_named_list "int control_fd" "const char *owner" "uint32_t cursor" "struct cryptodesc_named_list_entry *entries" "uint32_t max" "uint32_t *count" "uint32_t *next_cursor"
.Ft int
.Fn cryptodesc_owner_list "int control_fd" "uint32_t cursor" "char (*owners)[CRYPTODESC_KEY_OWNER_MAX]" "uint32_t max" "uint32_t *count" "uint32_t *next_cursor"
.Ft int
.Fn cryptodesc_restrict "int descriptor_fd" "uint32_t rights"
.Ft int
.Fn cryptodesc_revoke "int descriptor_fd"
.Ft int
.Fn cryptodesc_get_info "int descriptor_fd" "struct cryptodesc_info *info"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
library is a thin wrapper around the crypto descriptor
.Xr ioctl 2
ABI declared in
.In sys/cryptodesc.h
and implemented by the
.Xr crypto 4
driver.
A crypto descriptor is a file descriptor of type
.Dv DTYPE_CRYPTO
that wraps exactly one OpenCrypto session or one kernel-resident asymmetric
key.
The descriptor fixes the session's algorithms and key material at mint time;
a holder can only submit the operations permitted by the descriptor's rights
mask and can never create further sessions or recover the key material through
it.
Descriptors are passable, so they may be handed to another process with
.Xr sendmsg 2
.Pq Dv SCM_RIGHTS
or delivered by the capability plane, and they remain usable in capability
mode
.Pq see Xr capsicum 4 .
.Pp
Every function returns zero on success and \-1 on failure with
.Va errno
set.
Arguments are validated in the library before any ioctl is issued; a request
that is malformed fails with
.Er EINVAL
without touching the kernel.
.Ss Control and descriptor file descriptors
.Fa control_fd
is an open
.Pa /dev/crypto
control descriptor
.Pq see Xr crypto 4 .
The minting functions
.Fn cryptodesc_mint ,
.Fn cryptodesc_mint_generated
and
.Fn cryptodesc_mint_key
may be issued on any control descriptor.
The named-key family
.Pq Fn cryptodesc_named_* No and Fn cryptodesc_owner_list
is privileged: the kernel accepts it only on a control descriptor opened by a
process that held
.Dv PRIV_DRIVER
at
.Xr open 2
time, and it trusts the
.Fa owner
supplied with each request.
In a production system the sole holder of that authority is the
.Dv system.Crypto
broker,
.Xr BSDCrypto 8 ,
which fills
.Fa owner
from the requesting client's unforgeable channel label; ordinary clients reach
named keys only through
.Xr libcryptocmp 3 .
.Pp
.Fa descriptor_fd
is a crypto descriptor previously returned by one of the minting or leasing
functions.
.Fn cryptodesc_restrict ,
.Fn cryptodesc_revoke
and
.Fn cryptodesc_get_info
operate on the descriptor itself and may be called by any holder, including
one that received the descriptor from another process.
.Ss Rights
A descriptor carries a
.Fa rights
mask built from the following bits, declared in
.In sys/cryptodesc.h :
.Bl -tag -width CRYPTODESC_RIGHT_EXCHANGE -offset indent
.It Dv CRYPTODESC_RIGHT_ENCRYPT
Submit
.Dv COP_ENCRYPT
cipher operations.
.It Dv CRYPTODESC_RIGHT_DECRYPT
Submit
.Dv COP_DECRYPT
cipher operations.
.It Dv CRYPTODESC_RIGHT_AUTH
Compute a MAC or digest
.Pq Dv COP_ENCRYPT No on a digest session .
.It Dv CRYPTODESC_RIGHT_VERIFY
Verify a MAC, digest or Ed25519 signature.
.It Dv CRYPTODESC_RIGHT_SIGN
Produce an Ed25519 signature
.Pq Dv CIOCCRYPTOSIGN .
.It Dv CRYPTODESC_RIGHT_EXCHANGE
Perform an X25519 key agreement
.Pq Dv CIOCCRYPTX25519 .
.It Dv CRYPTODESC_RIGHT_DERIVE
Derive a child session from the descriptor's secret
.Pq Dv CIOCCRYPTODESCDERIVE .
.El
.Pp
.Dv CRYPTODESC_RIGHT_SESSION
is the union of
.Dv ENCRYPT ,
.Dv DECRYPT ,
.Dv AUTH ,
.Dv VERIFY
and
.Dv DERIVE ,
the rights meaningful on a symmetric session, and
.Dv CRYPTODESC_RIGHT_ALL
adds
.Dv SIGN
and
.Dv EXCHANGE .
Every minting function requires a non-zero mask that is a subset of
.Dv CRYPTODESC_RIGHT_ALL .
.Pp
The kernel derives the rights an operation needs from the session mode:
a plain cipher needs
.Dv ENCRYPT
or
.Dv DECRYPT ;
a digest or MAC session needs
.Dv AUTH
to compute and
.Dv VERIFY
to check; an encrypt-then-authenticate or AEAD session needs
.Dv ENCRYPT | AUTH
to seal and
.Dv DECRYPT | VERIFY
to open.
A
.Dv CIOCCRYPT
or
.Dv CIOCCRYPTAEAD
request on a descriptor must carry a session id of zero and is refused with
.Er EPERM
when any required bit is missing.
.Pp
Rights only ever narrow.
.Fn cryptodesc_restrict
replaces the descriptor's mask with
.Fa rights ,
which must be a subset of the current mask and may be zero; there is no way
to restore a bit once it has been dropped, on this descriptor or on any
duplicate of it, because all duplicates share the same underlying object.
A holder that forwards a descriptor should therefore
.Xr dup 2
it and restrict the copy only when it also wants to keep the wider rights for
itself; otherwise restricting before passing narrows what the recipient can
do.
.Ss Minting ephemeral descriptors
.Fn cryptodesc_mint
creates a session from
.Fa session ,
a
.Vt struct session2_op
exactly as accepted by the
.Dv CIOCGSESSION2
ioctl of
.Xr crypto 4 ,
with the caller supplying the cipher and MAC keys through the
.Va key
and
.Va mackey
pointers; the key bytes are copied into the kernel during the call.
.Va ses
must be zero.
The resulting descriptor never expires.
It issues
.Dv CIOCGCRYPTODESC
with a
.Vt struct cryptodesc_create .
.Pp
.Fn cryptodesc_mint_generated
creates a session whose cipher and MAC keys are generated inside the kernel
and never enter any address space.
The
.Va key
and
.Va mackey
pointers of
.Fa session
must be
.Dv NULL ;
.Va keylen
and
.Va mackeylen
.Pq each at most 128 bytes
select how much material is generated.
.Fa ttl
is a lifetime in seconds after which the descriptor expires; zero means no
expiry.
It issues
.Dv CIOCGCRYPTODESCGENERATE
with a
.Vt struct cryptodesc_generate .
.Pp
.Fn cryptodesc_mint_key
generates an asymmetric key pair inside the kernel.
.Fa type
is
.Dv CRYPTODESC_KEY_X25519 ,
for which
.Fa rights
must be a subset of
.Dv CRYPTODESC_RIGHT_EXCHANGE ,
or
.Dv CRYPTODESC_KEY_ED25519 ,
for which
.Fa rights
must be a subset of
.Dv CRYPTODESC_RIGHT_SIGN | CRYPTODESC_RIGHT_VERIFY .
The public half is copied to the
.Dv CRYPTODESC_ED25519_PUBLIC_SIZE
.Pq 32
byte
.Fa public_key
buffer; the private half is retained only by the descriptor.
Key agreement, signing and verification are performed with the
.Dv CIOCCRYPTX25519 ,
.Dv CIOCCRYPTOSIGN
and
.Dv CIOCCRYPTOVERIFY
ioctls on the descriptor, which the library does not wrap.
It issues
.Dv CIOCGCRYPTOKEYDESC
with a
.Vt struct cryptodesc_key_create .
.Ss Named keys
A named key is a kernel-resident symmetric-key template identified by the pair
.Pq Fa owner , Fa name .
Both identifiers are 1 to
.Dv CRYPTODESC_KEY_NAME_MAX
.Pq respectively Dv CRYPTODESC_KEY_OWNER_MAX
minus one characters drawn from
.Ql A-Z ,
.Ql a-z ,
.Ql 0-9 ,
.Ql \&. ,
.Ql _
and
.Ql - ;
the library rejects anything else with
.Er EINVAL .
Named keys are volatile: they live only until deleted or until the
.Xr crypto 4
module is unloaded, and every operation on them is visible only under the
owner that created them.
Each named key carries a
.Em generation
counter that starts at one and advances on every rotation and on deletion.
.Pp
.Fn cryptodesc_named_create
creates
.Fa name
under
.Fa owner
from the algorithm profile in
.Fa session ,
whose
.Va key
and
.Va mackey
must be
.Dv NULL
and whose
.Va keylen
and
.Va mackeylen
.Pq at most 128 bytes each, at least one non-zero
select the amount of kernel-generated material.
.Fa rights
is the maximum any lease may hold and must be a non-empty subset of
.Dv CRYPTODESC_RIGHT_SESSION .
The initial generation is stored in
.Fa generation .
It issues
.Dv CIOCGCRYPTONAMEDKEY .
.Pp
.Fn cryptodesc_named_lease
mints a session descriptor from the named key's current material with
.Fa rights
.Pq a non-empty subset of the key's granted rights
and an optional
.Fa ttl
in seconds, storing the generation the lease is bound to in
.Fa generation
and the descriptor in
.Fa descriptor_fd .
A lease is tied to the generation it observed: once the key is rotated or
deleted the lease enters the
.Dv CRYPTODESC_STATE_KEY_INVALID
state and every further crypto operation on it fails with
.Er EACCES .
It issues
.Dv CIOCGCRYPTONAMEDLEASE .
.Pp
.Fn cryptodesc_named_rotate
regenerates the key material, advances the generation, invalidates all
outstanding leases and stores the new generation in
.Fa generation .
.Fn cryptodesc_named_delete
destroys the key, invalidates all outstanding leases and stores the final
generation in
.Fa generation .
They issue
.Dv CIOCCRYPTONAMEDROTATE
and
.Dv CIOCCRYPTONAMEDDELETE
with a
.Vt struct cryptodesc_named_control .
.Pp
.Fn cryptodesc_named_stat
is a read-only lookup: it fills
.Fa stat
with the key's granted
.Va cd_rights ,
current
.Va cd_generation ,
cipher and MAC selectors
.Va cd_cipher
and
.Va cd_mac
.Pq zero when absent
and key lengths
.Va cd_keylen
and
.Va cd_mackeylen .
No descriptor is minted, the generation is not advanced and no key material
leaves the kernel.
It issues
.Dv CIOCGCRYPTONAMEDSTAT .
.Pp
.Fn cryptodesc_named_list
enumerates the keys owned by
.Fa owner
one page at a time.
.Fa cursor
is zero to start the walk or a previous call's
.Fa *next_cursor .
Up to
.Fa max
entries are copied to
.Fa entries ,
each reporting a key's
.Va cd_name ,
.Va cd_generation
and granted
.Va cd_rights ;
.Fa *count
receives the number filled and
.Fa *next_cursor
the cursor for the following page, or zero when the owner's keys are
exhausted.
The kernel returns at most
.Dv CRYPTODESC_NAMED_LIST_MAX
entries per call and advances the cursor by that many, so
.Fa entries
should hold at least
.Dv CRYPTODESC_NAMED_LIST_MAX
elements: entries beyond
.Fa max
are discarded and are not revisited by
.Fa *next_cursor .
It issues
.Dv CIOCGCRYPTONAMEDLIST .
.Pp
.Fn cryptodesc_owner_list
enumerates the distinct owners that currently hold named keys, up to
.Dv CRYPTODESC_OWNER_LIST_MAX
per call, with the same
.Fa cursor ,
.Fa max ,
.Fa count
and
.Fa next_cursor
paging contract as
.Fn cryptodesc_named_list .
Unlike the other named-key calls it deliberately spans owners; it exists so a
reclaim agent can drop the keys of owners that no longer exist, and only owner
identifiers are returned.
It issues
.Dv CIOCGCRYPTOOWNERLIST .
.Ss Attenuation, revocation and introspection
.Fn cryptodesc_restrict
narrows the descriptor's rights to
.Fa rights
as described under
.Sx Rights .
It issues
.Dv CIOCSCRYPTODESCRIGHTS
with a
.Vt struct cryptodesc_restrict .
.Pp
.Fn cryptodesc_revoke
permanently disables the descriptor: it enters the
.Dv CRYPTODESC_STATE_REVOKED
state and every subsequent operation, including further attenuation, fails
with
.Er EACCES .
Revocation is idempotent and affects every duplicate of the descriptor in
every process.
It issues
.Dv CIOCCRYPTODESCREVOKE .
.Pp
.Fn cryptodesc_get_info
fills
.Fa info ,
a
.Vt struct cryptodesc_info ,
with the descriptor's fixed-layout metadata:
.Bl -tag -width cd_provider_flags -offset indent
.It Va cd_size
Set by the library to
.Fn sizeof "struct cryptodesc_info" .
.It Va cd_type
Zero for a session descriptor, otherwise the
.Dv CRYPTODESC_KEY_*
type.
.It Va cd_rights
The current rights mask.
.It Va cd_state
Zero or a combination of
.Dv CRYPTODESC_STATE_REVOKED ,
.Dv CRYPTODESC_STATE_EXPIRED
and
.Dv CRYPTODESC_STATE_KEY_INVALID .
.It Va cd_crid
The OpenCrypto provider id serving the session, or \-1 for a key descriptor.
.It Va cd_provider_flags
The provider's
.Dv CRYPTO_FLAG_*
classification.
.It Va cd_expires
Absolute expiry time in seconds since the Epoch, or zero when the descriptor
does not expire.
.It Va cd_generation
The named-key generation this lease is bound to, or zero for an ephemeral
descriptor.
.It Va cd_key_generation
The most recent named-key generation the descriptor has observed; it differs
from
.Va cd_generation
once the key has been rotated or deleted.
.El
.Pp
It issues
.Dv CIOCGCRYPTODESCINFO .
The same fields are exposed to
.Xr kinfo_getfile 3
and
.Xr procstat 1
as a pseudo-path with the
.Ql crypto
prefix.
.Ss Expiry
A descriptor minted with a non-zero
.Fa ttl
expires at
.Va cd_expires .
The kernel arms a timer at mint time, so expiry is reported through
.Xr kqueue 2
without waiting for a crypto request; any operation attempted after expiry
fails with
.Er ESTALE .
.Ss Event notification
Crypto descriptors support the
.Dv EVFILT_CRYPTODESC
.Xr kqueue 2
filter, declared in
.In sys/event.h .
The
.Va fflags
of the registration must be non-zero and a subset of
.Dv NOTE_CRYPTODESC_CTRLMASK ,
otherwise
.Xr kevent 2
fails with
.Er EINVAL .
The following events may be requested:
.Bl -tag -width NOTE_CRYPTODESC_KEY_ROTATE -offset indent
.It Dv NOTE_CRYPTODESC_RIGHTS
The rights mask was narrowed by
.Fn cryptodesc_restrict .
.It Dv NOTE_CRYPTODESC_REVOKE
The descriptor was revoked.
.It Dv NOTE_CRYPTODESC_EXPIRE
The descriptor's time-to-live elapsed.
.It Dv NOTE_CRYPTODESC_KEY_ROTATE
The named key backing this lease was rotated.
.It Dv NOTE_CRYPTODESC_KEY_DELETE
The named key backing this lease was deleted.
.El
.Pp
The filter is always edge-triggered
.Pq Dv EV_CLEAR No is implied .
A returned event carries the requested bits that fired in
.Va fflags ,
the descriptor's current rights mask in
.Va data ,
the generation the lease is bound to in
.Va ext[0] ,
the absolute expiry time
.Pq zero if none
in
.Va ext[1]
and the latest observed named-key generation in
.Va ext[2] .
.Dv NOTE_CRYPTODESC_REVOKE ,
.Dv NOTE_CRYPTODESC_EXPIRE ,
.Dv NOTE_CRYPTODESC_KEY_ROTATE
and
.Dv NOTE_CRYPTODESC_KEY_DELETE
are terminal: when one of them is reported the event also carries
.Dv EV_EOF
and is delivered once
.Pq Dv EV_ONESHOT .
A terminal condition that already holds when the filter is attached is
reported immediately.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
All functions return zero on success and \-1 on failure with
.Va errno
set to indicate the error.
On failure no descriptor is returned and the output arguments, other than
.Fa count
and
.Fa next_cursor
which are reset to zero, are unspecified.
.Sh ERRORS
The library itself fails with:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EINVAL
A file descriptor argument is negative, a required pointer is
.Dv NULL ,
.Fa max
is zero,
.Fa rights
is zero
.Pq except for Fn cryptodesc_restrict
or has bits outside
.Dv CRYPTODESC_RIGHT_ALL ,
a
.Fa name
or
.Fa owner
is not a valid identifier, or a session passed to
.Fn cryptodesc_mint_generated
carries key pointers.
.It Bq Er EPROTO
The kernel reported success but did not return a descriptor.
.El
.Pp
Otherwise the functions fail with the error returned by
.Xr ioctl 2 ,
including:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EBADF
.Fa control_fd
or
.Fa descriptor_fd
is not a valid open descriptor.
.It Bq Er ENOTTY
.Fa descriptor_fd
is not a crypto descriptor.
.It Bq Er ENOTCAPABLE
The descriptor lacks the
.Dv CAP_IOCTL
right or the ioctl is not permitted by
.Xr cap_ioctls_limit 2 .
.It Bq Er EINVAL
The session profile is unsupported or its key lengths are out of range;
.Va ses
is non-zero; a reserved field is non-zero;
.Fa type
is unknown or
.Fa rights
is not permitted for that
.Fa type ;
a named key profile has neither cipher nor MAC key material; or
.Fa control_fd
is not a
.Pa /dev/crypto
descriptor.
.It Bq Er EFAULT
A key pointer supplied to
.Fn cryptodesc_mint
is invalid.
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
No OpenCrypto provider supports the requested session.
.It Bq Er EPERM
A named-key operation was issued on a control descriptor that does not hold
descriptor authority; or
.Fn cryptodesc_restrict
attempted to add a right the descriptor does not hold.
.It Bq Er EACCES
The descriptor was revoked; a lease's named key was rotated or deleted; or a
lease requested rights the named key does not grant.
.It Bq Er ESTALE
The descriptor has expired.
.It Bq Er ENOENT
No named key
.Pq Fa owner , Fa name
exists.
.It Bq Er EEXIST
A named key
.Pq Fa owner , Fa name
already exists.
.It Bq Er ENOSPC
The system-wide or per-owner named-key limit
.Po
.Va kern.crypto.cryptokey_max_objects
and
.Va kern.crypto.cryptokey_max_owner_objects ,
16384 and 1024 by default
.Pc
has been reached.
.It Bq Er EIO
Kernel key generation failed.
.It Bq Er EMFILE
The process has no free descriptor slots.
.It Bq Er ENFILE
The system file table is full.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr procstat 1 ,
.Xr cap_ioctls_limit 2 ,
.Xr cap_rights_limit 2 ,
.Xr ioctl 2 ,
.Xr kqueue 2 ,
.Xr kinfo_getfile 3 ,
.Xr libcryptocmp 3 ,
.Xr capsicum 4 ,
.Xr crypto 4 ,
.Xr BSDCrypto 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
library and the crypto descriptor ABI first appeared in 5BSD.
